          "annotations": [],
          "logprobs": [],
          "text": "The pattern indexes as a primitive tetragonal cell with \\(a \\approx 4.120\\) \u00c5 and \\(c \\approx 9.660\\) \u00c5. The diagnostic reflections include 001 at 9.15\u00b0, 002 at 18.36\u00b0, 100 at 21.55\u00b0, 101 at 23.46\u00b0, 003 at 27.68\u00b0, 102 at 28.46\u00b0, 110 at 30.67\u00b0, and 111 at 32.07\u00b0.\n\nThe intensity relationships favor polar **P4mm (No. 99)** with \\(Z=1\\): Er and Br occupy the two fourfold axes, Bi occupies the twofold edge site, and oxygen occupies a fourfold mirror site. The heavy-atom arrangement is well constrained; the oxygen coordinates are less precise from Cu powder data alone and should be finalized by Rietveld refinement.\n\n### Primary structure CIF\n\n```cif\ndata_ErBi2BrO4\n_audit_creation_method            'Powder-pattern indexing and structure-factor solution'\n_chemical_name_common             'erbium dibismuth bromide oxide'\n_chemical_formula_sum             'Er Bi2 Br O4'\n_chemical_formula_structural      'ErBi2BrO4'\n_cell_formula_units_Z             1\n\n_symmetry_cell_setting            tetragonal\n_symmetry_space_group_name_H-M    'P 4 m m'\n_symmetry_Int_Tables_number       99\n\n_cell_length_a                    4.1197\n_cell_length_b                    4.1197\n_cell_length_c                    9.6600\n_cell_angle_alpha                 90\n_cell_angle_beta                  90\n_cell_angle_gamma                 90\n_cell_volume                      163.92\n\n_diffrn_radiation_type            'Cu Kalpha1'\n_diffrn_radiation_wavelength      1.5406\n\nloop_\n_symmetry_equiv_pos_as_xyz\n'x,y,z'\n'-y,x,z'\n'-x,-y,z'\n'y,-x,z'\n'-x,y,z'\n'x,-y,z'\n'y,x,z'\n'-y,-x,z'\n\nloop_\n_atom_site_label\n_atom_site_type_symbol\n_atom_site_symmetry_multiplicity\n_atom_site_fract_x\n_atom_site_fract_y\n_atom_site_fract_z\n_atom_site_occupancy\n_atom_site_U_iso_or_equiv\nEr1  Er  1  0.5000  0.5000  0.0000  1.0  0.006\nBr1  Br  1  0.0000  0.0000  0.6000  1.0  0.009\nBi1  Bi  2  0.5000  0.0000  0.2690  1.0  0.007\nO1   O   4  0.1700  0.1700  0.1000  1.0  0.012\n```\n\nThe inversion-related polar domain is obtained by \\(z\\rightarrow1-z\\): Bi \\(z=0.731\\), Br \\(z=0.400\\), and O \\(z=0.900\\). It gives the same conventional powder pattern and is not a distinct structural alternative. The approximate model gives Er\u2013O and Bi\u2013O distances near 2.15 and 2.24 \u00c5, respectively.",
